{
  "about": "The request mix of the gRPC variant of the release benchmark's definitions (bench/definitions-grpc/), which bench/bench.py sends when it serves that variant, in the case grpc-keep-alive. bench/gen_definitions.py writes it: a gRPC call to each method of the Mock shop, by weight, each with a Session of its own, the headers a gRPC client sends over HTTP/2, and its framed request message in a file under bench/ (`bodyFile`), which oha sends with -D. get-order is matched by a condition on the message and gets a static reply, quote-order a templated reply, and track-order NOT_FOUND, sent as Trailers-Only. Every call gets the HTTP status 200, which is all that oha sees; `expect.grpcStatus` is the gRPC status that the Journal records, which e2e/bench_test.mbt checks.",
  "requests": [
    {
